   Toolchains — the tools kit runs on, and what installs them

   ✅ bash 5.2 runs kit
   ❌ jq is not installed
      brew install jq
   ❌ several tool managers are usable for the project: mise, brew; choose one
      kit toolchains use mise
      or: kit toolchains use brew
   ❌ brew is installed but not on PATH
      eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv)"
      add it to your shell profile to keep it

   kit runs on four tools: bash, git, jq, and yq. This step checks each one. Then it checks the machine's package
   manager, such as brew or apt, which installs them.

   When a check fails, the line under it gives the command that fixes it, or says where to read more. Run the command
   yourself, or have kit run it and check again. kit runs nothing until you ask, and it never runs a command that has
   to run in your own shell.

   The tools a repository's work needs are its toolchain. Inside a repository, kit toolchains lists the toolchains kit
   finds and which one it chose. For how kit finds and chooses what installs the tools, read docs/toolchains.md
   (https://github.com/empowerite/kit/blob/main/docs/toolchains.md).

   kit toolchains











